# Copy to .env.local (which is gitignored) and set both values.
#
# The dashboard refuses every request until DASHBOARD_PASSWORD is set - it
# fails closed, so a missing value locks the door rather than opening it.
#
# This matters because `next start` binds every interface, so the dashboard is
# reachable from any device on your Wi-Fi. It serves a minute-by-minute record
# of what this person looked at and when.
#
# Rotating the password invalidates all existing sessions, because the session
# cookie is signed with this value. Restart the server after changing it.
DASHBOARD_PASSWORD=

# Bearer token the Android reporter sends with each push. Separate from the
# dashboard password on purpose: the phone has no login form, and putting the
# dashboard password on a device that leaves the house is a worse trade than a
# token that can be rotated on its own. It fails closed too.
#
# This must ALSO differ from the sibling Data Usage Tracker's token. Two apps
# on one phone pushing to two dashboards should not share a credential - and if
# one APK is ever rebuilt with the wrong endpoint, a distinct token turns a
# silent cross-write into a clean 401.
ANDROID_INGEST_TOKEN=
